WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.336 --> 00:00:18.639
Dressed as a beggar, Robin walked along the road for most of the afternoon.

2
00:00:18.659 --> 00:00:22.582
"I should head back to Sherwood Forest soon," he said.

3
00:00:22.602 --> 00:00:25.024
"But I'd like to have one more adventure."

4
00:00:26.745 --> 00:00:30.468
So he looked up and down the road, hoping to see someone approaching.

5
00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:34.706
Soon a thin man came riding along on a skinny horse.

6
00:00:35.627 --> 00:00:39.750
The man was wearing strange-looking clogs with very thick soles.

7
00:00:40.651 --> 00:00:42.052
Robin stared at the man.

8
00:00:42.072 --> 00:00:43.813
"I know him!"

9
00:00:44.154 --> 00:00:44.614
he thought.

10
00:00:44.634 --> 00:00:48.117
"That's the wicked corn merchant who cheated the poor!"

11
00:00:50.358 --> 00:00:53.581
The corn merchant had bought a huge supply of corn.

12
00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:57.524
Then he held onto it to create a corn shortage.

13
00:00:58.336 --> 00:01:03.139
When everyone in the village was desperate for corn, he sold it at a high price.

14
00:01:03.879 --> 00:01:06.841
And he'd done this greedy thing several times.

15
00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:11.303
When the merchant approached, Robin stepped into the road.

16
00:01:12.083 --> 00:01:15.225
"Stop!" cried Robin, grabbing the horse's reins.

17
00:01:15.245 --> 00:01:17.446
"Who are you?"

18
00:01:17.766 --> 00:01:18.827
demanded the merchant.

19
00:01:18.847 --> 00:01:21.568
"Just a poor beggar," said Robin.

20
00:01:22.109 --> 00:01:24.490
"Have pity and give me a few pennies for bread."

21
00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:26.631
"Get away from me!"

22
00:01:26.971 --> 00:01:28.092
yelled the corn merchant.

23
00:01:28.724 --> 00:01:31.066
"Beggars like you belong in prison."

24
00:01:31.086 --> 00:01:35.270
"We both take money from other people," said Robin.

25
00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:38.213
"Neither one of us does honest work.

26
00:01:38.713 --> 00:01:42.196
We're like brothers, except you're rich and I'm poor."

27
00:01:42.216 --> 00:01:44.899
"Don't talk to me like that!"

28
00:01:45.359 --> 00:01:47.081
said the corn merchant angrily.

29
00:01:47.101 --> 00:01:50.824
"As for giving you money, I don't have any.

30
00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:54.608
I don't dare travel near Sherwood Forest with money.

31
00:01:55.208 --> 00:01:58.550
That thief Robin Hood hasn't been captured yet!"

32
00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:02.131
Robin showed no reaction to his name.

33
00:02:02.911 --> 00:02:05.613
Instead he motioned for the merchant to bend down.

34
00:02:05.633 --> 00:02:08.014
"Look at me," he whispered.

35
00:02:08.034 --> 00:02:11.335
"There's not one bit of dirt on my face or hands.

36
00:02:11.855 --> 00:02:13.616
Do you really think I'm a beggar?

37
00:02:14.176 --> 00:02:15.517
I'm as honest as you are."

38
00:02:16.237 --> 00:02:20.519
Robin opened his shirt to reveal a small bag hanging around his neck.

39
00:02:21.139 --> 00:02:22.860
"I'm hiding this from Robin Hood."

40
00:02:24.104 --> 00:02:28.128
The merchant's eyes widened as Robin showed him some gold coins.

41
00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:31.010
"Put that money away, you fool!"

42
00:02:31.331 --> 00:02:32.031
said the merchant.

43
00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:36.035
"If Robin Hood catches you, he'll take everything you have.

44
00:02:36.615 --> 00:02:40.278
He hates dishonest beggars as much as greedy merchants."

45
00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:44.162
"Oh, I had no idea!"

46
00:02:44.522 --> 00:02:46.524
Robin pretended to be surprised.

47
00:02:46.544 --> 00:02:48.505
"May I walk with you?

48
00:02:49.006 --> 00:02:51.328
We seem to be going in the same direction."

49
00:02:51.892 --> 00:02:54.814
"Well, all right," said the corn merchant.

50
00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:59.336
"I don't mind your company, now that I know you're an honest man."

51
00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:09.863
The two men traveled in silence until they reached the outskirts of Sherwood Forest.

52
00:03:10.303 --> 00:03:12.004
Then the merchant turned to Robin.

53
00:03:12.024 --> 00:03:15.066
"We're getting close to where Robin Hood lives.

54
00:03:15.706 --> 00:03:18.668
Here's where you're in the greatest danger, my friend."

55
00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:23.561
"I wish I had as little money with me as you do," said Robin.

56
00:03:23.581 --> 00:03:26.522
"I'm afraid Robin Hood will steal my gold."

57
00:03:27.602 --> 00:03:29.963
The merchant laughed and winked at Robin.

58
00:03:29.983 --> 00:03:32.063
"I'll tell you a secret.

59
00:03:32.824 --> 00:03:35.464
I have more money with me than you do.

60
00:03:35.925 --> 00:03:40.386
But it's hidden in a place Robin Hood will never find."

61
00:03:41.266 --> 00:03:43.287
Robin opened his eyes wide.

62
00:03:44.067 --> 00:03:46.067
"Really?" The merchant nodded.

63
00:03:46.087 --> 00:03:48.068
"See my shoes?

64
00:03:48.756 --> 00:03:51.799
The soles of my clogs are actually boxes.

65
00:03:52.339 --> 00:03:55.862
I've hidden ninety pounds in gold coins in each one."

66
00:03:55.882 --> 00:03:58.604
"In the soles of your clogs?"

67
00:03:59.185 --> 00:04:01.427
Robin laughed until he cried.

68
00:04:03.889 --> 00:04:06.551
The merchant stared at Robin with a frown.

69
00:04:06.571 --> 00:04:08.953
"There's nothing to laugh at!"

70
00:04:09.453 --> 00:04:11.054
But Robin was still chuckling.

71
00:04:11.074 --> 00:04:13.837
"I really like those clogs.

72
00:04:14.417 --> 00:04:15.778
Take them off and give them to me.

73
00:04:16.459 --> 00:04:19.137
If you don't take them off, I'll summon my friends."

74
00:04:19.637 --> 00:04:21.198
The merchant turned pale.

75
00:04:21.218 --> 00:04:23.420
"Who are you really?"

76
00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:26.582
"Everyone calls me Robin Hood!"

77
00:04:27.463 --> 00:04:30.725
The merchant shook with fear as he removed his clogs.

78
00:04:31.405 --> 00:04:34.487
Robin made him open the soles and count out the coins.

79
00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:36.649
"Now get out of here!"

80
00:04:37.049 --> 00:04:38.310
Robin said sternly.

81
00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:42.113
"I've heard many stories about how you've cheated the poor.

82
00:04:42.753 --> 00:04:46.616
If I hear any more of these stories, you'll be in real trouble!"

83
00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:49.962
The merchant rode away as fast as he could.

84
00:04:51.604 --> 00:04:55.527
That night in Sherwood Forest the fire stayed lit for a long time.

85
00:04:56.167 --> 00:05:02.132
Around the glowing fire, Robin and Little John entertained the men with stories of their adventures as a

86
00:05:02.212 --> 00:05:03.213
beggar and a friar.

87
00:05:04.114 --> 00:05:06.876
The men listened closely, laughing at their tales.

88
00:05:07.596 --> 00:05:10.038
When they were finished, Friar Tuck spoke up.

89
00:05:10.058 --> 00:05:16.604
"I still believe that the life of the friar is happier than the life of the beggar."

90
00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:19.221
Will Scarlet shook his head.

91
00:05:19.241 --> 00:05:21.704
"I think Robin's day was more fun.

92
00:05:22.184 --> 00:05:24.906
He tricked those beggars and that nasty corn merchant."

93
00:05:25.667 --> 00:05:29.070
The other men quickly put in their opinions, arguing loudly.

94
00:05:30.832 --> 00:05:33.774
Some agreed with Friar Tuck, and others agreed with Will.

95
00:05:34.395 --> 00:05:36.897
But Robin and Little John just laughed.

96
00:05:37.558 --> 00:05:39.940
They'd both had entertaining adventures!
